            <div xml:id="d437">

                <pb facs="0606" n="518" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg518"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72115/3421: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-24T16:00:00-05:00"
                            >December 24, 1918—4 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>123. Legation Peking reports<anchor n="20" xml:id="d437-f1"/> that British and
                    French Legations are urging internment of all Austrians and Germans in China and
                    liquidation of enemy property. The Department has instructed Mr. Reinsch that in
                    its opinion such questions should await results of Peace Conference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
